 - **Retry.** `rate_limit`, `overloaded`, `network`, `timeout` and `server` retry with exponential backoff, at most 5 attempts, honouring `retryAfterMs`. `auth`, `bad_request`, `context_length` and `quota` (HTTP 402, or a 429 whose message says the plan or balance is spent) never retry. Each try is its own `attempt` event.
 - **Request event.** Carries model, effort, `toolsHash`, `systemHash`, `bodyHash`, TTL and header names with value hashes. Never header values.
 - **Role fallback** starts a new session on the fallback model; it never swaps the model inside a session (cache rule 5).
-- **Quota fallback.** A run that ends on a `quota` error continues on its fallback model (`--fallback`, then `fallback` in `~/.cedia/settings.json`, then the built-in `deepseek` → `anthropic/claude-haiku-5-5`; `none` turns it off; a repo cannot set it). The new session has `parentSession`, a logged reminder that the tree may hold part of the work, what is left of the turn and budget limits, and the first session's changed files as writes the done gate must still see verified. The result adds up both sessions' spend and turns.
+- **Quota fallback.** A run that ends on a `quota` error continues on its fallback model (`--fallback`, then `fallback` in `~/.cedia/settings.json`, then the built-in `deepseek` → `anthropic/claude-haiku-5-5`; `none` turns it off; a repo cannot set it). The new session has `parentSession`, a logged reminder that the tree may hold part of the work, what is left of the turn and budget limits, and the first session's changed files as writes the done gate must still see verified. The result adds up both sessions' spend and turns. `--on-quota wait:<minutes>` (or `onQuota` in user settings) waits in the same session for a `quota` error with a retry-after, up to that many minutes across the run, and falls back past that; a spent balance with no retry-after falls back at once. A history the provider refuses (`bad_request` or `context_length` after the session had an accepted request) restarts once in a new session on the same model, with the same inheritance as the fallback and a logged note; a resumed thread whose last session was refused starts a new one. Both record `why: 'rejected'` or the fallback's `quota`.
 - **Mid-conversation system prompt.** Appended as a system message when `midConversationSystem` is true, otherwise as a user text block.
 - **Parallel tools.** Calls whose `ToolSpec.effect` is `read` or `network` run in a bounded pool (8 at a time); `write_workspace` and `exec` run alone, as ordering barriers. `tool_intent` events are written in assistant block order; results go back as one batch (Anthropic requires all results of a turn in one user message).
 - **Permission order in the log.** `assistant → permission → tool_intent (only if allowed) → tool_result`. A denied call gets `tool_result{status:'denied'}` and no `tool_intent`.
